      "content": "# Analysis\n\nThe warning occurs because `ProjectDetailt.vue` (likely a fragment or teleport component) receives the `class=\"w-full\"` attribute from `ChatSidebar.vue`, but cannot inherit it due to its internal structure.\n\n**Root Cause:** The `ProjectDetailt` component needs to explicitly accept and apply class attributes to its root element.\n\nLet me request missing information:\n\n1. Can you share the `ProjectDetailt.vue` file content?\n2. Can you share the `ProjectSelectorContent.vue` file content?\n\nIn the meantime, I can provide a temporary fix for `ChatSidebar.vue` by removing the class attribute and wrapping the component:\n\n```vue src/components/chat/ChatSidebar.vue\n<template>\n  <!-- ... existing code ... -->\n  \n  <!-- Root Chat Card -->\n  <div class=\"px-1 shrink-0\">\n    <div\n      class=\"p-2 md:p-3 rounded-lg border-2 cursor-pointer transition-all hover:border-warning hover:bg-warning/5\"\n      :class=\"selectedChatId === rootChat.id \n        ? 'border-warning bg-warning/10' \n        : 'border-base-content/10 bg-base-200'\"\n      @click=\"selectChat(rootChat)\"\n    >\n      <!-- Project Selector -->\n      <div class=\"mb-2 z-50 w-full\">\n        <ProjectDetailt\n          :iconify=\"false\"\n          :modelValue=\"targetProject\"\n          :options=\"{ showFolders: false, showIcon: true, showSelector: true }\"\n          @update:modelValue=\"$emit('select-project', $event)\"\n        />\n      </div>\n      <!-- ... rest of template ... -->\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</template>\n```\n\n**Changes Made:**\n| Change | Location | Reason |\n|--------|----------|--------|\n| Moved `class=\"w-full\"` to parent wrapper div | ProjectDetailt usage | Prevents non-props attribute warning by applying width to container instead of component |\n\nPlease share the `ProjectDetailt.vue` and `ProjectSelectorContent.vue` files so I can provide a permanent fix that properly handles class inheritance.",
