      "summary": "# Conversation Summary\n\n1. **Problem Identified:** Vue warning about extraneous `class` attribute passed to `ProjectDetailt` component, which couldn't inherit it due to rendering fragment/text nodes.\n\n2. **Root Cause:** `ProjectDetailt.vue` was directly rendering `ProjectSelector.vue` (a multi-root component), preventing proper class attribute inheritance from parent components.\n\n3. **Solution Implemented:** Wrapped `ProjectSelector` in a single `<div class=\"w-full\">` root element in `ProjectDetailt.vue` to properly receive and inherit attributes.\n\n4. **Additional Fix:** Updated `ChatSidebar.vue` to apply the `w-full` class to a parent wrapper `<div>` instead of the component itself, following Vue3 best practices.\n\n5. **Result:** Eliminated Vue warning while maintaining component functionality and proper class attribute inheritance throughout the hierarchy.",
